      <LINES>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT>U1</TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE>&amp;FUNCTIONALITY&amp;</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE>The /CTDI/CL_PRINT_CUST_ENGINE class is the central configuration and</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE> validation engine for the dynamic repair printing framework. It resolves</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE> customizing definitions and manages development environment tasks.</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT>U1</TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE>FEATURES</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT>AS</TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE>This class contains key operations to:</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT>B1</TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE>- Resolve custom print drivers via an in-memory buffer, matching</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE>  Contract, SKZ, and AKZ fallbacks in /CTDI/REP_FORMS.</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT>B1</TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE>- Gated SE24 print subclass skeleton generator that checks client</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE>  modifiability (TR_SYS_PARAMS) and authority S_DEVELOP before stubs</TDLINE>
       </item>
       <item>
        <TDFORMAT></TDFORMAT>
        <TDLINE>  are generated in DEV.</TDLINE>
       </item>
      </LINES>
     </item>
